+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                 |
+| ------ | --------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress           |
+
+Every tool call passes through `ToolRegistry.execute`, which makes it the one place the declared `inputSchema` can become something the engine enforces rather than something it merely forwards to the providers. This spec states what the registry promises about the input it hands an executor, what a tool author may assume about input that reaches them, and how a call the schema rejects is reported back to the model.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs; a call the schema rejects never reaches the executor and is returned as a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure instead of throwing ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property, names the requirement, and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L56)).
+- Input the schema accepts reaches the executor unchanged, unlisted extra properties included, exactly as it was received: no injected defaults, no coercion, and exactly one executor call per `execute` ([validated by: passes input the schema accepts through to the executor unchanged, extra properties included, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
+- A rejection message names the failing property path and the constraint that failed, and neither that message nor any log line the rejection produces carries a property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field by path and expected type, and carries no field value in the message or the logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once, at `register` time, and `execute` does not compile it again ([validated by: compiles a static tool schema once, at register time](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L150)).
+- A schema the validator cannot compile makes `register` throw at registration time with an error naming the tool, so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time for a schema the validator cannot compile, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L107)).
+- A schema produced by a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call and is validated against the schema current at that call, cached by the resolved schema object ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L124)).
+- A rejected tool call is fed back to the provider as tool-result text the model can read and correct, so a message that rejects one call and retries with corrected input resolves rather than ending the conversation with a generic error ([validated by: feeds a rejected tool call back to the provider as text the model can correct](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L172)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only: it does not inject `additionalProperties: false` or apply defaults ([validated by: passes input the schema accepts through to the executor unchanged, extra properties included, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
+- A value of the wrong declared type is rejected rather than coerced into the type the schema names ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field by path and expected type, and carries no field value in the message or the logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+- `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name; the rejection contract covers schema failures only ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L215)).
+
+## Documentation
+
+- The JSON Schema validator is declared in `package.json` `dependencies`, reading the same schema format handed to the providers rather than introducing a second, hand-written one.
+- `docs/adding-a-tool.md` tells tool authors that input reaching an executor has already passed the declared schema, that unknown keys may still be present, and that a rejection is returned to the model rather than thrown; `README.md` and `.specify/spec.md` state the same.
+- `CHANGELOG.md` carries an entry for this change, written for a consumer of the published package.
